curriculum-vitae - my CV in LaTeX
=================================
This repository contains my curriculum vitae, written in LaTeX. There
is one source file per language: an English version (en_cv.tex) and a
Romanian version (ro_cv.tex).


Requirements
------------
In order to build the CV you need a TeX distribution with pdflatex
(TeX Live is what I use). The sources use these packages: fullpage,
titlesec, enumitem, hyperref, fancyhdr, tabularx, color and babel
(with Romanian support for ro_cv.tex). A full TeX Live installation
includes all of them; with a smaller one, install the missing
packages with tlmgr.


Building
--------
Run pdflatex on the file of the language you want:

    pdflatex ro_cv.tex

The resulting ro_cv.pdf and the auxiliary files are created in the
same directory. The same works for en_cv.tex. latexmk can be used
instead:

    latexmk -pdf ro_cv.tex


Editing
-------
Each file is split into a preamble, which defines the layout and a
few custom commands, and the content, which starts after the "CV
content" comment. Entries are written with these commands, for
example \resumeSubheading for a job or project and \resumeItem for a
bullet point.

The small version tag in the footer of the page is set with
\cvversion at the top of each file.


Files
-----
    en_cv.tex   English version of the CV
    ro_cv.tex   Romanian version of the CV
    .gitignore  keeps build files out of Git


Credits
-------
The layout is based on https://github.com/sb2nov/resume (MIT
license).
